            <ArticleTitle>Serving the underserved: school-based asthma intervention programs.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>463-72</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Asthma is a common and costly disease, which disproportionately affects young, ethnic minority, and impoverished individuals. A heightened public awareness has catalyzed a variety of efforts to reduce the impact of childhood asthma in the United States. Despite these efforts, however, at-risk groups continue to suffer excess morbidity. Strategies are required that can specifically address the needs of underserved communities. We review the underlying rationale and progress of school-based programs designed to assist asthmatic children.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
